Looking at this problem, I need to write a SystemVerilog testbench for `clk_ratio_div` that measures `clk_o` edges in time (not sampled values), drives everything from `clk_i`, and handles odd divisors correctly. The "What to produce" section has copy-paste errors from a different problem (id_width_conv), so I'll write the appropriate testbench for `clk_ratio_div`.

Key design decisions:
- Use edge recorders (`always @(posedge clk_o)`) pushing timestamps to queues, polled from `clk_i` — this captures exact edge times without clocking the TB from `clk_o`
- Measure period/duty in raw time (handles odd divisors' half-integer phases)
- Measure G1 from `div_ready_o` rise, not `div_valid_i` assertion
- Use `drain_all` before measurements to avoid stale queue entries

```systemverilog
