If the poller runs first, `rise_cnt` is not yet incremented. The poller doesn't see the rise. It will see it at the next poll.

So the poller either sees the rise at time T (if recorder first) or at time T+10 (if poller first). In both cases, `t_rise` is T (the correct time). The only issue is if `clk_o` rises again at T+10 before the poller checks. In that case, `t_rise` would be T+10 (the second rise), and the poller would incorrectly report T+10 instead of T.

